`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The telltale sign that a doc page isn't truly versioned is testing a deliberately wrong tag/path alongside the real one. A 301 that redirects regardless of the version segment (`4.2.x`, `9.9.x`, anything) to the same unversioned target means the site literally has no per-version content there — only a genuine 404 on a bad path proves the server is actually resolving per-version routes. Pulsar's Docusaurus docs clearly version the broker/admin content but share the client-library pages across all versions, so templating `documentation-url` with `$version$` would have silently pointed every tested version at today's "latest" docs — exactly what the task rules forbid.
